# COPY . . in docker/Dockerfile is meant to bring in scripts/, data/golden_dataset,
# etc. for ad-hoc use inside the container -- not the local dev environment.
# Without this file, that COPY also swept in .venv/ (715MB) and data/corpus/
# (192MB, gitignored raw filings), bloating the build context past 1GB and
# breaking the image export outright; and, more seriously, .env itself,
# which would have baked real API keys into an image layer.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git/
.github/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.DS_Store
*.log

.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Large, gitignored, reproducible via scripts/pull_sec_corpus.py -- not
# needed at runtime (retrieval hits Pinecone, not these raw files).
data/corpus/
data/xbrl/
data/raw/
data/raw_meta/
data/index_cache/
